+++ b/KIO-FORK.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# KIO Sound full native fork
+
+Independent KIO fork of the complete [SoundCraft v0.7.0](https://github.com/storytold/soundcraft/releases/tag/v0.7.0) workspace at immutable commit `3a28a657692c1b98b28c276d8f61df9471074f0f`. Based on SoundCraft by the ArtCraft team; no upstream endorsement. This source retains every supplied native engine, format, rendering, UI, CLI, MCP, collaboration and web module. It does not establish parity with the commercial application that inspired upstream.
+
+## Patch scope
+
+Display/window/About strings, existing product-name translations, application identity, installer metadata and per-user profile defaults use `KIO Sound` / `com.kio.sound`. Crate and binary machine names, commands, native file-format identifiers, dependency pins and content behavior remain intact. The original KIO `public/kio-program-icons/sound.png` is converted to platform sizes/formats. ArtCraft trademark logo/mark files and README logos are removed; original trademark conditions remain in `docs/brand/LICENSE-brand.txt`. All original code licenses, NOTICE, contributor/model credits and asset attribution are retained, with KIO artwork provenance added. Platform branding exceptions: none outside desktop and UI layers.
+
+## Exact build inputs
+
+[KIO-FORK.json](KIO-FORK.json) records source archive and original KIO icon SHA-256 values, the fixed font input (none requested by upstream), features and full app/CLI build arguments. Use Rust 1.95 and the committed lock file. Preserve all defaults and original upstream release features. The reusable binary Git patch and per-file before/after hash manifest live beside the source archive and in the KIO native build patch registry. The parent build stage handles platform builds, signing and output verification.
+
+## Inherited limitations
+
+Pre-alpha. The pinned release includes device/sample-rate/buffer selection, but input-channel routing and duplex-latency depth remain limited. Live MIDI-controller recording and AAF/OMF session interchange are not supplied. Third-party plug-in compatibility, real-world recording stability and DAW parity are not independently validated. All original gap, localization and format-parity documents remain authoritative for this pinned release. No original feature has been intentionally removed, and no upstream gap is represented as resolved.
+
+## Verification state
+
+Static checks compare protected engine/dependency/license/credit files byte for byte, validate platform metadata and icon formats, and reapply the patch to a separate fresh original source extraction with complete resulting file-hash comparison. This branding agent did not build, install or run the resulting app. Native launch, open/save, printing/export, plug-ins, recovery and profile isolation still require build and GUI QA before release.
